fans were delighted to see patrick  stewart reprise his role as professor x  in the latest dr strange movie but there  was one easter egg that most viewers  missed here is the x-men tease and  doctor strange 2 only hardcore fans  noticed it's been a long time coming but  doctor strange in the multiverse of  madness is finally here the bold new  chapter of the marvel cinematic universe  pushes the master of the mystic arts  further than ever before as he's thrown  into different realities in his fight to  save america chavez from being killed by  a supernatural entity like many big  blockbusters of the last few years it  was met with production delays due to  the pandemic but the sequel finally  gives fans the live-action multiversal  adventure they've been looking for  thanks to chavez's powers steven strange  is a little wiser this time around  although he's mourning the life he could  have had with christine palmer who gets  married just as the adventure begins the  idea that there are alternate worlds  where he winds up being with christine  as a tantalizing idea for the sorcerer  and it's a sentiment scarlet witch  shares in this turn as the surprising  main villain wanda maksimov is looking  for a universe where she can be with her  sons billy and tommy after the events of  wandavision but the adventure across the  multiverse sees dr strange meet a  mysterious council of heroes who have  sworn to protect their universe and  beyond the illuminati fans already got a  glimpse of the team in the trailers  recognizing patrick stewart's voice and  the iconic yellow chair from the comics  and animated series we can now gladly  confirm he reprises his role as  professor x but there's another  surprising x-men tease in the scene and  this one only hardcore fans noticed it  was only a matter of time before we  started to get major x-men characters in  the mcu after disney bought fox back in  2019 as most fans will already know the  x-men and fantastic four franchises  exist in their own separate universes  although deadpool makes plenty of jokes  about marvel comics and the mcu with his  signature fourth wall breaking humor  let us go talk to the professor  mcavoy or stewart these timelines are so  confusing  although many expected marvel to simply  reboot the x-men to fit the mcu the  studio is clearly taking a slightly  different approach since patrick stewart  returns from the original movies to play  charles xavier again although this time  he's in the yellow hover chair  the illuminati will see you now  when the film first introduces the  illuminati it's an incredibly surprising  scene and professor x's late arrival  only adds to the spectacle especially  because the theme song from the original  x-men animated series heralds his debut  it's worth pointing out that this isn't  the first time we've seen an x-men star  show up in the mcu to reprise their role  evan peters returns his quicksilver in  wandavision although it's later revealed  as a fake out peters is actually a  normal man named ralph boner at least  professor x is actually who he says he  is here albeit a marginal multiversal  variant the theme song is a real treat  for hardcore fans and it comes with  another surprising detail buried in the  end credits when looking at the  multiverse of madness credits there's an  interesting detail in the music section  it lists the iconic theme music as x-men  97 theme this suggests that the upcoming  x-men 97 animated revival series will  use the original theme song when it  arrives on disney plus in the near  future it's entirely possible that x-men  97 is set to take place on the same  version of earth that the illuminati  live on in doctor strange in the  multiverse of madness or they might  exist in their own version of reality  for now it's anyone's guess but the  multiverse does open up so many  possibilities for franchises that  weren't previously connected to the  ongoing tapestry of the mcu obviously  there's a fantastic four movie in  development at the moment but it's not  clear whether john krasinski will  reprise his role as reed richards from  the film or if it'll be someone  completely different the same can also  be said for patrick stewart and  professor x whenever marvel eventually  releases a proper x-men movie  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you
 

